--------------------------------------------------
External knowledge that might be helpful: 
The assumptions include:
- consider only those series that have CT modality and do not belong to the NLST collection
- filter out DICOM images that use the following two compression formats:
    - JPEG Lossless, Non-Hierarchical, First-Order Prediction, 1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70;
    - JPEG Baseline (Process 1), 1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51;
- do not contain localizer image type
- all instances in a series have identical values for image orientation (patient) and pixel spacing (converted to string before comparison)
- all instances in a series have 1 ± 0.01 as the dot product between the two vectors below:
    - cross product of first and second vectors;
    - vector [0, 0, 1];
- have number of instances in the series equal to the number of distinct values of Image Position (Patient) attribute (converted to string for comparison)
- all instances in a series have identical values for the first two components of Image Position (Patient)
- all instances in a series have identical pixel rows, and similarly identical pixel columns
- for the difference between the values of the 3rd component of Image Position (Patient), after sorting all instances by that third component


BTW, the desired output report should contain:
1. The unique identifier for each image series;
2. The number assigned to the series within a study;
3. The unique identifier for the study that the series belongs to;
4. The unique identifier for the patient;
5. The maximum dot product value between the cross product of image orientation vectors and a reference vector, indicating geometric alignment;
6. The total number of SOP instances (individual images) in each series;
7. The number of distinct slice thickness values within the series;
8. The maximum and minimum difference between consecutive slice intervals (the z-coordinate spacing);
9. The tolerance value for slice interval differences (the z-coordinate spacing);
10. The number of distinct exposure values;
11. The maximum and minimum exposure value recorded for the images;
12. The difference between the maximum and minimum exposure values within the series, indicating the range of exposure variation;
13. The total size of the image series in megabytes (MiB).
And please sort the final output by slice interval difference tolerance, maximum exposure difference and series unique ID (all in descending order).
The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'IDC': {'IDC_V17': ['DICOM_ALL']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below is a short “data–discovery cheat‑sheet” that shows  

• which DICOM columns are likely to be useful for every filter / metric that your final report will need,  
• the main logic (Boolean conditions) you will probably apply, and  
• ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (LIMIT 20 each) that you can run in sequence to acquaint yourself with the data before writing the big production query.

────────────────────────────────────────
POSSIBLY RELEVANT COLUMNS AND THEIR ROLES
────────────────────────────────────────
"collection_name"                 : keep / remove whole collections (exclude ‘NLST’)  
"Modality"                         : select ‘CT’ series only  
"TransferSyntaxUID"                : filter out two JPEG syntaxes  
"ImageType"                        : detect “LOCALIZER” strings  
"SeriesInstanceUID"                : the series identifier (report item 1)  
"SeriesNumber"                     : series number inside a study (item 2)  
"StudyInstanceUID"                 : study identifier (item 3)  
"PatientID"                        : patient identifier (item 4)  
"ImageOrientationPatient" (VARIANT): six reals – orientation vectors (geometry tests, item 5)  
"ImagePositionPatient"   (VARIANT) : three reals – z‑spacing checks  
"PixelSpacing"           (VARIANT) : two reals – must be identical in a series  
"Rows","Columns"                   : identical size check  
"SliceThickness"                   : item 7 – #distinct values  
"Exposure"                         : items 10‑12 (min/max/range)  
"instance_size"                    : bytes -> MiB, item 13  
"SOPInstanceUID"                   : counting SOP instances  
"InstanceNumber" / "ImageIndex"    : useful for ordering slices  

────────────────────────────────────────
CONDITIONS THAT WILL APPEAR IN THE FINAL QUERY
────────────────────────────────────────
1. Modality                              = ‘CT’  
2. collection_name                      != ‘NLST’  
3. TransferSyntaxUID NOT IN (‘1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70’, ‘1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51’)  
4. UPPER(ImageType) NOT ILIKE ‘%LOCALIZER%’  
5. Per‑series tests (to be done with HAVING / QUALIFY):  
   • COUNT(DISTINCT ImageOrientationPatient::STRING)             = 1  
   • COUNT(DISTINCT PixelSpacing::STRING)                        = 1  
   • COUNT(DISTINCT Rows) = 1 AND COUNT(DISTINCT Columns) = 1  
   • COUNT(*) = COUNT(DISTINCT ImagePositionPatient::STRING)  
   • COUNT(DISTINCT (ImagePositionPatient[0]::STRING, ImagePositionPatient[1]::STRING)) = 1  
   • MAX( ABS( (ImageOrientationPatient[0]::FLOAT * ImageOrientationPatient[4]::FLOAT)  
               - (ImageOrientationPatient[1]::FLOAT * ImageOrientationPatient[3]::FLOAT) ) )  
       ≈ 1  ( dot‑product requirement)  

────────────────────────────────────────
TEN STEP‑BY‑STEP EXPLORATORY QUERIES
────────────────────────────────────────
```sql
--1️⃣  Description: Peek at the most frequent modalities to be sure ‘CT’ exists.
SELECT "Modality", COUNT(*) AS "cnt"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
GROUP BY "Modality"
ORDER BY "cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2️⃣  Description: Distinct transfer syntaxes that appear in CT images (not NLST).
SELECT DISTINCT "TransferSyntaxUID"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "Modality" = 'CT'
  AND "collection_name" <> 'NLST'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3️⃣  Description: Inspect CT rows that use any JPEG syntax we must exclude.
SELECT "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "TransferSyntaxUID",
       "ImageType",
       "collection_name"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "Modality" = 'CT'
  AND "TransferSyntaxUID" IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70',
                              '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4️⃣  Description: Find common values of ImageType for CT to locate LOCALIZER patterns.
SELECT UPPER("ImageType"::STRING) AS "img_type", COUNT(*) AS "cnt"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "Modality" = 'CT'
GROUP BY UPPER("ImageType"::STRING)
ORDER BY "cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5️⃣  Description: Sample orientation & spacing values for one random CT series.
SELECT "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "ImageOrientationPatient",
       "PixelSpacing",
       "Rows",
       "Columns"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = (
      SELECT "SeriesInstanceUID"
      FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
      WHERE "Modality" = 'CT'
            AND "collection_name" <> 'NLST'
      LIMIT 1)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--6️⃣  Description: Check per‑series counts of distinct orientation strings
--     to see how many series already satisfy the single‑orientation rule.
SELECT "SeriesInstanceUID",
       COUNT(*)                           AS "inst_cnt",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "ImageOrientationPatient"::STRING) AS "orient_distinct"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "Modality" = 'CT'
  AND "collection_name" <> 'NLST'
GROUP BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "ImageOrientationPatient"::STRING) > 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--7️⃣  Description: Compute the dot‑product check for a few slices of one series.
SELECT "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "SOPInstanceUID",
       /* components 0..5 correspond to the two direction vectors */
       ("ImageOrientationPatient"[0]::FLOAT * "ImageOrientationPatient"[4]::FLOAT
        - "ImageOrientationPatient"[1]::FLOAT * "ImageOrientationPatient"[3]::FLOAT) AS "dot_with_k",
       "ImageOrientationPatient"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = (
      SELECT "SeriesInstanceUID"
      FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
      WHERE "Modality" = 'CT'
            AND "collection_name" <> 'NLST'
      LIMIT 1)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--8️⃣  Description: Verify that SOP count equals distinct ImagePositionPatient count.
SELECT "SeriesInstanceUID",
       COUNT(*)                                   AS "sop_cnt",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "ImagePositionPatient"::STRING) AS "pos_cnt"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "Modality" = 'CT'
  AND "collection_name" <> 'NLST'
GROUP BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
HAVING COUNT(*) <> COUNT(DISTINCT "ImagePositionPatient"::STRING)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--9️⃣  Description: Collect slice‑thickness and z‑spacing statistics for each series.
SELECT "SeriesInstanceUID",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "SliceThickness")                  AS "distinct_thk",
       MIN("SliceThickness")                             AS "min_thk",
       MAX("SliceThickness")                             AS "max_thk",
       MIN( "ImagePositionPatient"[2]::FLOAT )           AS "min_z",
       MAX( "ImagePositionPatient"[2]::FLOAT )           AS "max_z"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "Modality" = 'CT'
  AND "collection_name" <> 'NLST'
GROUP BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--🔟  Description: Quick view of exposure stats & total size (MiB) for CT series.
SELECT "SeriesInstanceUID",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "Exposure")                        AS "distinct_exposure",
       MIN(TRY_TO_NUMBER("Exposure"))                    AS "min_exposure",
       MAX(TRY_TO_NUMBER("Exposure"))                    AS "max_exposure",
       (MAX(TRY_TO_NUMBER("Exposure")) - MIN(TRY_TO_NUMBER("Exposure"))) AS "exp_range",
       ROUND(SUM("instance_size") / 1048576, 2)          AS "series_size_MiB"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE "Modality" = 'CT'
  AND "collection_name" <> 'NLST'
GROUP BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries should give you a solid understanding of the data distribution and help you craft the final production SQL that puts all the geometry and quality filters together and returns the requested report fields, ordered by slice‑interval tolerance, exposure range, and series UID (all descending).
